{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>לחה.</b> The heh in place of vav, like בתוך אהלה, from the root לח, for dryness overcomes the old." "And the meaning of <b>נס.</b> is the opposite of נתת."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 34, :notes {0 "The lemma לחה is from ולא כהתה עינו ולח לא נס in Deut 34:7; Ibn Ezra reads לחה with a suffixed heh in place of the expected vav-conjunctive."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:26:41.850545644Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}